== 2026-11-20 15:17:59 #1025 P1-prime: lambda_1 on backgrounds re-solved at u0 0.02 (Ks 30), D 16, k_c 55 and 63. Written before the run.
Why: u0test_note.log. At fixed states the premise failed, so only re-solved backgrounds measure the horizon truncation's effect on lambda.
The coordinator approved this in its hc message after 14:42 UTC.
Runs (lane_u0r.sh, venv-314, wip/ell1-highD 139e29d2 code, from solver/matter of choptuik-1025):
  A: ell_refine.py l1kc55Fb1025 55 l1kc55Fh1025 55 1 16 2.2426280416106374 --kappa 0.7 --u0 0.02 --Ks 30 --tol 1e-12 --wait 60
  B: ell_refine.py l1kc63Fm1025 63 l1kc63Fh1025 63 1 16 2.2459627535552045 --kappa 0.7 --u0 0.02 --Ks 30 --tol 1e-12 --wait 60
  then on each new state: signtest.py around=<record>:16:0.02 --u0=0.02 --Ks=30 (raw I1025-mac/signtest.py, checked in c1_scan_note.log).
Record checks (as for every record): n_signchanges 1, within 2% of the guess, and the u0-aware signtest agrees on both sides. A record that
fails any of them is not read.
Shift d = lambda(u0 0.02) - lambda(u0 0.04 record), per k_c. Its noise: the float64 det sign is noise over ~1.6e-4 around the k_c 55 root
(c1_scan_note.log), so a float64 root is good to about 1e-4.
Bars for a shift to count as the horizon truncation's effect:
  T1 (measurable): |d| >= 3e-4 (3x that noise). Below it, the result is "no effect above 3e-4" at that k_c.
  T2 (scaling, the cut alone): a third record changes only the cut, Ks 45 at u0 0.04 (segment unchanged), if the series holds at order 45
     (my check before it starts: the dd series' A2 residual at u0 0.04 with Ks 45, and the float64 block 12 at Ks 45 against the dd one at
     Ks 45 no worse than at Ks 30); otherwise u0 0.03 (tag Fi), which also lengthens the segment. With r the predicted truncation ratio
     (Ks 45 or u0 0.03 residual over the u0 0.04 Ks 30 one, from the dd A2 measurement), the third root must satisfy
     |lambda_3 - lambda(u0 0.02)| <= max(0.2 |d|, 3e-4) when r <= 1e-2. If it stays near the u0 0.04 value instead, the shift is not
     the cut's.
  The coordinator's rule, applied only if T1 and T2 pass: if |d| exceeds the k_c spread at D 16 (the 55 -> 63 move, 3.33e-3), the k_c
  sequences so far mix the two errors, and every lambda past D 15 needs u0 0.02 (or Ks raised) before any k_c reading.
Also reported: d(63) - d(55) against the 55 -> 63 move at u0 0.04 (+3.33e-3), i.e. the k_c move at u0 0.02.
Note on the coordinator's Ks 45 estimate (~1e-8 at k_c 63, D 16): the u^30 fit gives the residual's dependence on u at fixed Ks, not on Ks,
so it does not predict Ks 45. The dd A2 at Ks 45 measures it instead.
